[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am trying a form of \"deferred implementation\". It would be convenient if I can define an instance in such a way as to take priority over a variable. Concretely, the following works fine and as expected:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"o\">](</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 10</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>However, the following gives an error because the variable instance is taking priority:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"o\">](</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: Cannot evaluate, contains free variable `dc` -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Adding the <code>default_instance</code> attribute also does not help. I would be grateful for suggestions or insights. I can redesign so that I do not introduce the variable command, but not having to do that will help. To clarify I am generating code meta-programmatically (otherwise I would simply fix by hand).</p>",
        "id": 616243347,
        "sender_full_name": "Siddhartha Gadgil",
        "timestamp": 1786603337
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Local instances like your <code>dc</code> variable always take priority. Can you use a <code>section</code> to restrict the scope of the variable?</p>",
        "id": 616386600,
        "sender_full_name": "Francisco Giordano",
        "timestamp": 1786647513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You could achieve this by having two separate classes like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"o\">](</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dc</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: Cannot evaluate, contains free variable `dc` -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DoubleClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">doubleFn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">double</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 616398874,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1786651723
